  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Two sources of light emit with a power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>. The ratio of number of photons of visible light emitted by each source having wavelengths <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo> </mo><mi>nm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo> </mo><mi>nm</mi></math> respectively, will be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> be the number of photons coming out from the first and the second source of light respectively per second.</p><p>So, for the first source,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And, for the second source,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equations (1) and (2), it implies that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>300</mn><mn>500</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}